lifeos-nix patch f-inference-provider — local model server, Anthropic as fallback

PROBLEM
  LifeOS can only talk to Anthropic. `claude` is the sole model client, and Inference.ts
  actively deletes ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL. There is no way to run on a local LLM server, and no
  way to keep Anthropic as a safety net — or to forbid it — when one is used.

FIX
  One file in the USER zone, LIFEOS/USER/CONFIG/inference.conf, one `key=value` per line:

    mode=local-only                  # anthropic-only | local-with-fallback | local-only
                                     # (no mode + base_url set: local-with-fallback)
    base_url=http://host:port        # must speak Anthropic /v1/messages
    model=name                       # all tiers; model_fable/opus/sonnet/haiku override
    token_env=VAR                    # optional; not an ANTHROPIC_* variable

  - The lifeos-nix claude wrapper (pkgs/tools/misc/claude-code/claude-gate.sh) reads the file
    ONCE, in shell, from the account's passwd home (never $HOME, LIFEOS_* or CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR),
    and everything decides from that one text. No file or mode=anthropic-only: exec the real
    claude, no bun, the upstream path. Local modes: the text goes to `InferenceProvider.ts gate`
    on stdin (no second read), which must agree with the wrapper's mode and writes the env delta
    plus a sentinel on fd 3; the wrapper execs in place. `claude --lifeos-gate-query` prints the
    wrapper's reading for Inference.ts and never reaches the real binary.
  - NEW LIFEOS/TOOLS/InferenceProvider.ts — parses the same line format (parseConf), decides
    the env per exec, maps tiers to local model names, health-checks for local-with-fallback.
  - Inference.ts: local-with-fallback retries once on Anthropic when the local attempt fails
    (with fallbackTimeoutMs when the caller set one); local-only fails closed. Spawns carry
    LIFEOS_INFERENCE_TARGET so the gate honours the choice. The executed model is verified by
    its local name.

WHY THIS SHAPE (Klemen, 2026-10-07)
  The gate ROUTES. It does not enumerate what Claude Code can do that reaches Anthropic
  (subcommands, flags, settings sources, providers): that surface changes every release, and
  review rounds kept finding gaps in such lists. Reading the mode out of LIFEOS_CONFIG.toml
  through caller-steerable paths and text heuristics kept being misread too, hence its own file
  in a format shell can read exactly. The local-only guarantee belongs to the network room (ISA
  Step 7c). Kept because they are static and cheap: a base_url that is not an Anthropic host;
  Bedrock/Vertex/Foundry routing off on the local target; under local-only NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC
  on, WebFetch off and claude.ai MCP off.

FAIL-CLOSED
  - Absent file (ENOENT, and no link to nothing on the path) is anthropic-only; any other read
    error, a line that is not a comment or known_key=value without spaces, a repeated key or a
    bad value refuses. CR is dropped and NUL becomes a space on both sides.
  - A CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR install with its own inference.conf refuses (ambiguous).
  - local-only never fails over; an Anthropic hint under local-only refuses.
  - A local mode without a gate file, any gate error, a missing sentinel (e.g. a stale payload)
    or an env delta that does not apply refuses. The gate runs from / with --config=/dev/null
    and --no-env-file.
  - LIFEOS_GATE=off (manual) is refused when the file says local-only or gives no mode.

VERIFIED GOTCHA (why AUTH_TOKEN is always set on the local target)
  With only ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL set, Claude Code sends the subscription OAuth bearer token to
  that URL (measured 2026-10-04). AUTH_TOKEN outranks OAuth, so a server without auth gets
  "lifeos-local-no-auth", never the subscription credential.

KNOWN LIMITS
  An API-key-only user's fallback has no key (the Anthropic leg runs on the subscription).
  Without fallbackTimeoutMs a fallback can take the local timeout plus the Anthropic timeout.
  --config=/dev/null on the gate has no observable effect today (bun loads no global bunfig
  for `bun file.ts`, and the gate runs from /); it stays as a guard.
  Claude Code itself can still reach Anthropic outside the gate's view: the network room's job.

VERIFICATION
  tests/inference-provider/run.sh — 81 tests against the pinned source + patch list and the
  real gate script, in env -i with a fake passwd (never the runner's own home): parsing and
  refusals, shell/TS agreement on the same bytes, env overlay/strip, the decide() table, the
  gate end to end (no-bun fast path, env steering, invalid/unreadable files, dangling links,
  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, SHELLOPTS, bunfig preload, stale payload, readonly var, health cache,
  GATE=off, unresolvable uid), Inference.ts through the wrapper query. Mutation-checked.

